Table dcim_cabletype {
  id uuid [pk, note: 'default in Python: uuid4()']
  created "timestamp with time zone" [note: 'default in Python: now()']
  last_updated "timestamp with time zone" [note: 'default in Python: now()']
  _custom_field_data jsonb [not null, note: 'default in Python: dict()']
  name varchar(255) [unique, not null]
  description varchar(255) [not null]
  manufacturer_id uuid
  part_number varchar(255) [not null, note: 'Discrete part number (optional)']
  has_embedded_transceivers boolean [default: false, not null, note: 'Indicates that this cable type has transceivers (e.g. SFP) built in.']
  a_connectors smallint [default: 1, not null, note: 'Number of physical connectors on the A side.']
  b_connectors smallint [default: 1, not null, note: 'Number of physical connectors on the B side.']
  total_lanes smallint [default: 1, not null, note: 'Total number of logical lanes in the breakout, distributed evenly across connectors on each side.']
  mapping jsonb [not null, note: 'A→B lane mapping as a JSON array of objects with keys: label, a_connector, a_position, b_connector, b_position. If empty, will be auto-populated.. default in Python: list()']
  is_shuffle boolean [default: false, not null, note: 'Indicates non-linear (polarity-shuffled) position mapping. Informational only.']
  strands_per_lane smallint [default: 1, not null, note: 'Number of physical strands per logical lane (e.g. 1 for copper, 2 for duplex fiber).']
  polarity_method CableTypePolarityMethod [default: '', not null, note: 'Fiber polarity method. Informational only.']

  indexes {
    (name) [name: 'dcim_cabletype_name_2d321d6d_like', note: 'varchar_pattern_ops']
    (manufacturer_id) [name: 'dcim_cabletype_manufacturer_id_49e6bbe2']
  }

  Note: '''A reusable definition of a kind of cable.

Includes (for breakout cables) internal lane structure, connectors on each side,
the total number of logical lanes, and the A-to-B lane mapping for the breakout.

By convention and by model enforcement, any breakout is A-to-B, not B-to-A; that is, `a_connectors` may never be
greater than `b_connectors`, though they may be equal. `total_lanes` must be evenly divisible by both
`a_connectors` and `b_connectors`; the implied per-side positions per connector are derived from that division.

Columns from ChangeLoggedModel (abstract): created, last_updated.

Columns from CustomFieldModel (abstract): _custom_field_data.

Columns from BaseModel (abstract): id.'''
}

